<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Jan 1-25 palm oil exports 401,932t-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Jan 1-25 palm oil exports 401,932t-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for January 1-25 at 401,932 tonnes against 589,456 in December 1-25.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 86,504 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 164,186 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 52,889 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 98,353 tonnes.  </p>
<p>India, which was the main buyer during the period, taking 72,470 tonnes, Pakistan 53,372 tonnes, China 25,505 tonnes and Indonesia 24,160.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 95,655 tonnes. -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
</text>
